one;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">THE SQUAD</span></h2><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">A settled spine, an unsettled back four, and a left wing in limbo</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Arteta&#39;s selection questions for Cardiff are almost entirely defensive. Everything from the base of midfield forwards has, if anything, too many answers.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>Begin with what is certain. </span><span style="font-weight:700">David Raya</span><span>&nbsp;returns as first choice and as a World Cup winner, having been part of the </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Spain</span><span>&nbsp;squad that beat </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Argentina</span><span>&nbsp;1-0 after extra time in the final in July. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Kepa Arrizabalaga</span><span>&nbsp;and the newly arrived </span><span style="font-weight:700">Illan Meslier</span><span>, a free transfer from the relegated </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Leeds United</span><span>, complete a three-deep goalkeeping department. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Rice</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Zubimendi</span><span>&nbsp;are the base. </span><span style="font-weight:700">&Oslash;degaard</span><span>&nbsp;is the captain and, along with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Martinelli</span><span>, was given an extended break after international duty. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Gy&ouml;keres</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Havertz</span><span>&nbsp;returned early after </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Sweden</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Germany</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;exited the World Cup at the group and early knockout stages respectively, and both have looked sharp.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The defensive picture is the whole story. Fifteen </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;players went to the World Cup, representing nine nations &mdash; the largest contingent from any Premier League club, and a direct cause of the compressed, ragged pre-season the champions have had. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Saliba</span><span>&nbsp;came back from it with a back complaint that is now open-ended. Arteta&#39;s phrasing &mdash; two weeks of doing &quot;almost nothing&quot;, then a reassessment &mdash; is the language of a club that does not yet know. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Timber</span><span>&nbsp;had groin surgery in June and will miss both the Shield and the opening weekend. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ben White</span><span>&nbsp;is fit but has been fragile for two years. That is the entirety of the argument for spending &pound;50m-plus on </span><span style="font-weight:700">Konsa</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;in the last three weeks of a window.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>Tactically, two threads are worth watching on Sunday. The first is the height of the line: without </span><span style="font-weight:700">Saliba</span><span>&#39;s recovery pace, the risk profile of </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&#39;s pressing scheme changes materially, and both </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Betis</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Dortmund</span><span>&nbsp;scored goals in the first half-hour that looked like the system rather than the individuals. The second is set pieces at both ends. </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;have been the league&#39;s most productive dead-ball side under </span><span style="font-weight:700">Nicolas Jover</span><span>; in pre-season they have been conceding from them, with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Gadou</span><span>&#39;s goal for </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Dortmund</span><span>&nbsp;coming from a corner </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;defended badly. Champions do not usually regress in the one area they have monopolised. It is worth watching whether the return of the full first-choice group fixes it.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>Forward, the shape of the front line has quietly changed. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Tzolis</span><span>&nbsp;has started pre-season on the left, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Bukayo Saka</span><span>&nbsp;is back in training after the World Cup and is untouchable on the right, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Gy&ouml;keres</span><span>&nbsp;leads the line with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Havertz</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Merino</span><span>&nbsp;behind him, and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Eze</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">&Oslash;degaard</span><span>&nbsp;rotate through the ten. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Noni Madueke</span><span>&nbsp;gives width on either flank. That leaves </span><span style="font-weight:700">Martinelli</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jesus</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;&mdash; two Brazilians with title medals &mdash; as the squad&#39;s most saleable assets and its most obvious sources of August friction.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Injury &amp; Availability</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">William Saliba:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Back. In &quot;rest mode&quot;, doing almost nothing for two weeks. No return date. Out for Cardiff.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Jurri&euml;n Timber:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Groin surgery (June). &quot;Still weeks away.&quot; Out for Cardiff and the opener.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Louie Copley:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Ruptured ACL v Real Betis, Aug 5. Out long-term.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Ben White:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Returning to full fitness after two injury-affected seasons. Available.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Returned:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">Raya</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Rice</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Saka</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Merino</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Zubimendi</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Gabriel</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;back in training post-World Cup.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="font-weight:700">Rested:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">&Oslash;degaard</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Martinelli</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;given extended breaks; both expected available.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">HALE END</span></h2><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Dowman at 16, Julienne at right-back, and a golden boot in Shanghai</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">A brutal blow for Louie Copley, a genuine emergence for Theo Julienne, and an academy season that starts this Saturday.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The hardest news first. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Louie Copley</span><span>, the 18-year-old midfielder whose progress had been one of the quiet pleasures of </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&#39;s summer, confirmed on August 7 that he ruptured his anterior cruciate ligament in the defeat to </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Real Betis</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, having been withdrawn after ten minutes. &quot;The road ahead won&#39;t be easy,&quot; he wrote, &quot;but I&#39;ll give everything to come back stronger.&quot; He will miss the season.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>His absence has opened a door for </span><span style="font-weight:700">Theo Julienne</span><span>. The 18-year-old, a midfielder who became a fixture in the U21s during the second half of last season, has featured in every first-team friendly and made his Emirates debut off the bench against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Dortmund</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; largely at right-back, a position he has taken to out of necessity with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Timber</span><span>&nbsp;out and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Copley</span><span>&nbsp;gone. Arseblog&#39;s assessment is that he &quot;has always carried the aura of a senior professional.&quot; He started against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Como</span><span>&nbsp;on Wednesday alongside </span><span style="font-weight:700">Marli Salmon</span><span>, with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Max Dowman</span><span>&nbsp;also in the XI and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Josh Ogunnaike</span><span>&nbsp;among the substitutes. On Tuesday, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Julienne</span><span>&nbsp;trained with the first team alongside </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ife Ibrahim</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Demiane Agustien</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;&mdash; Ibrahim and Julienne singled out as the two who have most impressed.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Dowman</span><span>&nbsp;remains the headline act. Sixteen years old, a goal and an assist in the 4-1 win at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Girona</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, and a starter rather than a cameo in three of the four friendlies. He made his Premier League debut last season. There is no sensible version of this campaign in which he is not involved with the senior squad.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>Abroad, </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&#39;s U17s were declared joint winners of the Shanghai Future Star Cup on August 9 after the final was cancelled by a typhoon. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jaden Maghoma</span><span>&nbsp;took the golden boot with four goals and an assist, having scored in a 1-1 draw with </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Athletic Club</span><span>&nbsp;on August 6 from an </span><span style="font-weight:700">Emerson Nwaneri</span><span>&nbsp;assist; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Abraham Owusu-Gyasi</span><span>, who is chasing a professional contract, scored the decisive penalty in a 4-3 shootout win over </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Shanghai FA</span><span>&nbsp;in the semi-final. Separately, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Nathan Tchoumba</span><span>, a 15-year-old defensive midfielder from the </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Colorado Rapids</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;academy, trained with the U18s in a friendly this week before returning to MLS.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Academy Diary</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">U18s open:</span><span>&nbsp;Saturday, August 15 &mdash; away at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">West Bromwich Albion</span><span>. Season ends May 8 at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Reading</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">U21s open:</span><span>&nbsp;Saturday, August 22 &mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Crystal Palace</span><span>, Mangata Pay UK Stadium. Premier League 2, revised format; no fixture v </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Manchester United</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;this season.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Loan watch:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span